Add namespaces to the git backend

The idea is to have multiple "workspaces" in sub-paths in the git refs. You can switch
namespaces with a `tsk switch` command or something similar. Namespaces have plaintext
names and can be referenced from other namespaces using [[namepace/tsk-XX]] links. If no
namespace is specified in a [[]] link it is assumed to be the current namespace.
Additionally, you should be able to send tasks from one namespace to another namespace.
To do so, we need to introduce the concept of an "inbox" which is where tasks that are
"sent" to another namespace go. Tasks in the inbox can be listed and "accepted", which
turns them into tasks in the local namespace, assigning them a new ID. As extended
metadata, tasks that have been accepted from the inbox should have a "source" reference
linking them to the original task that was "exported" from the source namespace.